<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Kestrel Software Ltd's capitalisation table before and after the Series A, as at 24 September 2026, sent to Ashcombe Reeve
  LLP by Ines Kowalczyk (1003.1 Due Diligence). Every result is a real formula, and each formula cell also carries the value it
  works out to (office:value), which LibreOffice shows until it recalculates. If a figure changes, change the cached value beside it.
  The sums, for checking by hand:

    before  4,600,000 + 3,400,000 + 600,000 + 400,000 = 9,000,000 ordinary; 640,000 + 360,000 = 1,000,000 options; 10,000,000 in all
    Series A  1,875,000 + 625,000 = 2,500,000 shares at 1.60 = 4,000,000.00 (3,000,000.00 and 1,000,000.00)
    after  10,000,000 + 2,500,000 = 12,500,000; pre-money 10,000,000 x 1.60 = 16,000,000.00; post-money 12,500,000 x 1.60 = 20,000,000.00
    Series A investors 2,500,000 / 12,500,000 = 20.00%; Ines 4,600,000 / 10,000,000 = 46.00% before, 4,600,000 / 12,500,000 = 36.80% after
-->
